  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid Response Fund for Sudden Emergencies in Northeast Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After more than 13 years of conflict, violence, and insecurity, Northeast Nigeria continues to remain a large-scale humanitarian and protection crisis, affecting millions of people in the region as well as cross-border. Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) residing in camps and host communities continue to experience limited access to basic services, crowded living conditions, significant protection risks, and exclusion from participating in or benefitting from the humanitarian services. These conditions are closely linked to conflict-induced and recurrent population displacement and are also a result of pre-existing low levels of services to address these concerns in the northeast. Moreover, the effects of climate change are evident in Nigeria compounding people&apos;s existing vulnerabilities. IOM is contributing to the decreased vulnerability of populations affected by acute crises in Northeast Nigeria by strengthening the capacity of local partners for future humanitarian responses. IOM is establishing the Rapid Response Fund (RRF) to rapidly disburse funds to local partners, addressing the funding shortage and efficiently respond to the pressing needs of IDPs, returnees and vulnerable host community members. This involves capacity building in Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Shelter and Non-Food Item (NFI), Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), Protection, and Multi-purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA).</narrative>
  </description>
